# Survey & classification of the non-NS/YM root Agda modules

This document surveys the repository's **root-level** Agda modules (the 40 `*.agda`
files in the project root), which are *outside* the Yang–Mills / Navier–Stokes
"closure" stack already mirrored in the `ClayClosure` Lean library. Each module is
classified as **genuine provable content** or **structural scaffolding**, and its
Lean-mirror status is recorded.

The mirrors live in `AgdaMirror/` and are wired into the `AgdaMirror` Lean library
target (see `lakefile.toml`). Everything marked *proved* below genuinely compiles
and is axiom-clean (every theorem depends only on the permitted kernel axioms
`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` — most depend on none or only
`propext`). No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `@[implemented_by]`, no vacuous restatement.

## Honesty boundary

Agda `postulate`s are *assumptions*, not theorems. They are **never** transcribed
as Lean `axiom`s. Instead the assumed carriers/laws become explicit parameters and
structure fields (honest hypotheses), exactly as the existing closure files treat
their deep open inputs. Where the underlying claim is in fact genuinely provable
(e.g. the 3-adic identity, `ℤ/6` von Neumann regularity, no-infinite-descent),
it is *proved* rather than assumed — turning that scaffolding into genuine content.

